depgraph: one memo table per slot-operator probe (no functional change)

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 6 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs 0001, 0004, 0005 only.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: context only (the similar_available hunk, after the adaptation of 0005)

The probe memo of patches 0001, 0004 and 0005 was one dict with tagged
tuple keys. It becomes an object with one dict per probe
(_ProbeMemo: select_atoms_probe, upgrade_available, downgrade_probe,
similar_available), which is the form the tested build has and the form the
probe changes below extend. Same keys, same lifetime (one
_slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls call), no change in what is remembered.

On top of patches 0001-0012, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 41.8 -> 41.2, holds 24.1 -> 23.5, masks 45.2 -> 44.5,
  py313 27.2 -> 27.0, bdeps 31.9 -> 31.9, policykit 24.2 -> 24.0
  sum of six 194.4 -> 192.2 (-2.2 s, -0.5 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0013 together: 447.5 -> 192.2 s (-57 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Kept apart from 0014 so that the functional change there is not mixed with a
restructuring. This is the replacement of the reduced forms of 0001, 0004
and 0005. The small step is plausibly the single dict lookup per probe (the
tagged tuple keys were hashed twice per hit); it was not investigated.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
